<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Base manifest for the IT! Android head. Almost everything is generated from
    assembly attributes (the launcher activity, MonoRuntimeProvider, and the
    permissions in Permissions.cs) and merged into this file — this exists only to
    add the one thing that has no attribute form: <queries>.

    This comment used to say INTERNET came "from MSBuild items". It did not. There
    is no <AndroidPermission> build item, so no permission ever arrived that way and
    nothing warned. The app shipped with no INTERNET permission at all until
    2026-07-31 and nobody noticed, because every model had been sideloaded over adb.
    Permissions are declared in Permissions.cs as [assembly: UsesPermission].

    Android 11+ (API 30) package visibility: without this, CircleAI's
    contentResolver.Call to the out-of-process espeak G2P provider returns null
    (the package is invisible), so on-device TTS would silently fall back to
    text-only on newer phones. The P30 Lite is API 29 (Android 10), where visibility
    is not enforced, so this is forward-compat — scoped to the ONE provider authority
    CircleAI needs, nothing else.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
	<queries>
		<provider android:authorities="com.bhengubv.espeakng.g2p" />
	</queries>
	<application android:allowBackup="true" />
</manifest>
